new('ropinirole','Oral immediate-release ropinirole tablets','CrCl · mL/min','HD doses differ for Parkinson’s disease and restless legs.','Label §§2.2/2.3/8.6: no renal change at CrCl 30–50; severe impairment without regular HD is unstudied. ER is excluded. Dialysis RLS trials are not a universal indication for secondary RLS.',[('CrCl 30–50','No renal adjustment of the indication-specific regimen'),('CrCl <30 without regular HD','Not studied; no regimen selected')],flag='monitor')
drugs['ropinirole']['modalities']['ihd']=dict(status='summarized',tables=[table('Parkinson’s disease · IR tablets',[('Regular HD','Start 0.25 mg three times daily; titrate to response, maximum total 18 mg/day')]),table('Restless legs syndrome · IR tablets',[('Regular HD','Start 0.25 mg once daily; titrate to response, maximum total 3 mg/day')])],notes='No supplemental dose after dialysis is required by the selected label. Confirm indication and tolerate titration.',sourceIds=['spl111-ropinirole'])
new('amantadine','Oral immediate-release amantadine hydrochloride capsules','Label indexed CrCl · mL/min/1.73 m²','IR renal intervals can extend to once weekly.','Selected IR capsule label: do not apply these doses to extended-release products. The source uses indexed CrCl units. Accumulation can be profound; review age, cognition and toxicity.',[('CrCl 30–50','200 mg on day 1, then 100 mg daily'),('CrCl 15–29','200 mg on day 1, then 100 mg every other day'),('CrCl <15','200 mg every 7 days')])
mode('amantadine','ihd','Immediate-release capsule label',[('HD','200 mg every 7 days')],'Negligible HD removal; do not add an automatic post-HD replacement dose.')
new('memantine','Oral immediate-release memantine solution · 2 mg/mL','Cockcroft–Gault CrCl · mL/min','Severe renal impairment has a 5 mg twice-daily target.','Selected solution label: start at 5 mg daily and titrate no faster than weekly. Severe-impairment target applies to IR only. Do not extrapolate below CrCl 5, to ESRD/dialysis or to XR products. Urine alkalinisation can increase exposure.',[('Mild / moderate renal impairment','No renal reduction of the usual titrated regimen'),('CrCl 5–29','Target 5 mg (2.5 mL of this 2 mg/mL solution) twice daily')])
new('rivastigmine','Oral rivastigmine tartrate capsules','Moderate / severe renal impairment','Lower tolerated doses may be needed.','Capsule label §§2.4/8.6: titrate according to individual tolerability. No fixed CrCl dose table or dialysis prescription is provided; patch kinetics and dosing are separate.',[('Moderate / severe impairment','Titrate individually; a lower dose may be the maximum tolerated')],flag='monitor')
new('clonazepam','Oral KLONOPIN tablets','Renal impairment · no numeric cutoff','Use cautiously because metabolites are renally excreted.','Selected label: renal-disease PK has not been studied and no numeric renal adjustment is specified. Individualise cautiously; do not infer absence of adjustment or renal safety from that gap.',[(GEN,'Use cautiously to avoid metabolite accumulation; no numeric adjustment specified')],flag='monitor')
new('lorazepam','Injection · ATIVAN selected excipient-containing product','Renal disease versus renal failure · reconcile label warnings','Acute-dose wording does not establish safety in renal failure.','The selected injection label says an acute dose need not be adjusted in renal disease, but separately does not recommend use in renal failure. Frequent doses require caution; propylene glycol / polyethylene glycol toxicity is more likely with renal impairment. These restrictions require clinical reconciliation; no numeric renal or dialysis prescription is selected.',status='specialist',flag='monitor')
new('midazolam','Injection · selected IV / IM midazolam product','Renal impairment / AKI · no fixed CrCl algorithm','Renal impairment can delay recovery, particularly after infusions.','Selected label warns of slower elimination and accumulation of hydroxylated glucuronide metabolites. Reduce and titrate in high-risk patients under respiratory monitoring. No fixed renal percentage, infusion ceiling or post-HD supplement is supplied.',[(GEN,'Individualise and titrate cautiously; anticipate prolonged sedation and recovery')],flag='monitor')
new('tizanidine','Oral ZANAFLEX tablets / capsules','CrCl · mL/min','Below CrCl 25, use smaller individual doses during titration.','Label §2.3: if escalation is required, increase the individual dose rather than frequency. No fixed percentage or dialysis schedule. Ciprofloxacin and fluvoxamine are contraindicated interacting medicines; formulations and food effects differ.',[('CrCl <25','Use lower individual doses while titrating; increase the individual dose before frequency')])
new('phenobarbital','Oral phenobarbital tablets · selected label','Impaired renal function · no numeric cutoff','Reduce the dose in renal impairment.','Selected tablet label’s dosage section requires reduction but provides no renal percentage or routine HD/PD supplement. This label is for a marketed unapproved drug; presence on DailyMed is not FDA approval. Use measured levels and clinical monitoring with specialist input.',[(GEN,'Reduce the dose; the label supplies no numeric renal fraction')],flag='monitor')
new('brivaracetam','Oral BRIVIACT / IV','Renal impairment versus ESRD undergoing dialysis','No renal adjustment outside dialysis; use on dialysis is not recommended.','Label §8.6: ESRD undergoing dialysis lacks data and use is not recommended. Do not transfer the 2018 handbook’s normal-dose dialysis advice into this entry.',[('Renal impairment, not on dialysis','No renal dose adjustment required')],flag='monitor')
